      "narration": "Priya sponsors a softball team and buys blanket accident coverage. Blanket insurance covers a changing group of people exposed to a common hazard without naming each one: a team’s players, passengers on a bus, students at a school, campers at a summer camp. No individual certificates are issued because the members change. Benefits usually pay medical expenses from accidents during the covered activity. Blanket coverage is group coverage in form, but it insures a category of people rather than enrolled individuals, and that difference is the point the exam tests.",
