      "title": "Short-term medical in Maryland",
      "narration": "Short-term limited duration policies bridge gaps, such as the weeks between jobs. They are medically underwritten, exclude pre-existing conditions and need not include essential health benefits. Federal rules allow longer terms, but Maryland is stricter: a short-term policy sold in Maryland may last less than three months and may not be renewed or extended. Theo’s client who leaves a job in May should compare a short-term plan with a special enrollment on Maryland Health Connection or Maryland continuation coverage, which provide comprehensive benefits. Short-term coverage is a stopgap, and the notice must say so.",
